# `o[k]` under the key of this turn where a call stands between the step and the read: what the step saw of the object does not hold behind the call, so the test asks the
# enumerator and the object again, behind it the read is a load by the place of the key, and the read as written is the other arm
# function sum(o, f) { let s = 0; for (const k in o) { f(); s += o[k]; } return s; }
